  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Dappen. Execute deal+dapp setup, enforce follow-suit and trump rules, then score by trick points.',
    Player: 'As lone dappener, choose a safe lead that preserves your high trump controls for later key tricks.',
    objective: 'The lone player (Dappener) aims to win at least half of the total card points available (typically 40 or 41 points) by capturing tricks containing high-value cards.',
    gameplay: "1. Bidding/Dapping: Players must 'dappen' if they hold high trumps (Gstieß, 21, or 20). If most pass, the second-to-last player must take the Dapp.\n2. Talon usage: The lone player picks up the 12-card Dapp, adds it to their hand, and then discards 12 cards (scoring them for their team). 5-point cards cannot be discarded.\n3. Trick-taking: The lone player leads the first trick. Players must follow suit. If unable, they must play a trump. If they have neither, they may play any card.\n4. Winning: The highest trump wins the trick, or the highest card of the led suit if no trumps are played.",
    keyRules: [
      'Compulsory Dapping for high trump holders.',
      'Must follow suit if possible.',
      "No obligation to win the trick (no 'overruff' rule).",
      'One player plays against a cooperative team of all others.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
