    turnFlow: "1. Bidding/Dapping: Players must 'dappen' if they hold high trumps (Gstieß, 21, or 20). If most pass, the second-to-last player must take the Dapp.\n2. Talon usage: The lone player picks up the 12-card Dapp, adds it to their hand, and then discards 12 cards (scoring them for their team). 5-point cards cannot be discarded.\n3. Trick-taking: The lone player leads the first trick. Players must follow suit. If unable, they must play a trump. If they have neither, they may play any card.\n4. Winning: The highest trump wins the trick, or the highest card of the led suit if no trumps are played.",
